# electron-vite output. Unlike drove/web this is never read from git: desktop:package rebuilds it
# immediately before electron-builder runs, so committing it only adds churn to every diff.
web/out/

# Built UI assets ARE committed. The install path is `uv tool install git+...`, which builds the
# wheel from this source tree — so anything not in git is not in the install. Building at install
# time instead would put Node on the critical path for every user, which is exactly what shipping
# the UI inside the Python package was meant to avoid. Rebuild with `cd web && npm run build`.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.gstack/
